  "name": "scatter_tamil",
  "description": "Tamil consonants on the standardized 12-column place axis. Tamil's inventory is famously SYMMETRIC: one voiceless stop per place across 6 distinct places (bilabial ப, dental த, alveolar ற, retroflex ட, palatal ச, velar க) AND one matching nasal per place (ம ந ன ண ஞ ங). Voicing is allophonic, not phonemic — a signature of southern subcontinental phonology. Two lateral approximants (alveolar ல, retroflex ள), the unique Tamil retroflex approximant ழ /ɻ/ (the *zha* of *Tamiḻ*), the alveolar tap ர, and the glides வ, ய. 18 cells filled.",
